codex
A plausible low-cost correction is at the scored layer: keep the sample estimate, but blend in a Gaussian ReLU moment computed from the same sampled preactivation mean/variance. I’m adding it behind a constant so the evaluator tells us whether the bias/noise tradeoff is favorable.
